// Automaton spire: the precursor guardian at each of the inner band's gates (GDR-0116; GDR-0026, GDR-0099 A7). A
// long spine of three sections, each on two automaton cores of its own and joined by one bridge block: the head with
// two torpedo launchers, the body round a fusion reactor with two rocket pods on its flanks, the tail with the torch
// drive, a fission reactor and two rocket pods covering its back. Four prism wards (grown Lattice crystal, GDR-0027)
// stand along it and take energy fire whole but let most shells and missiles through, so a laser fleet barely
// scratches it. Shot apart, each section fights on alone; the head and body without the tail's drive turn but
// barely move. PLACEHOLDER layout (lead default, 19 Oct 2026, docs/results/spire-balance-2026-10-19.md). Not tagged
// `enemy`: the test range's waves keep to the rim's (GDR-0089).
(
    id: "automaton_spire",
    name: "Automaton spire",
    summary: "The inner band's gate guardian: a long three-section spine with torpedoes and rockets under crystal wards that turn lasers.",
    description: "Its four [[part:prism_ward|prism wards]] take laser fire whole and let most of a shell or a warhead through: bring [[part:reverse_engineered_cannon|cannons]] or [[part:rocket_pod|missiles]]. Its head throws [[part:torpedo_launcher|torpedoes]] from further than most guns reach, and [[part:rocket_pod|rocket pods]] cover its flanks and its back, so [[part:point_defence]] earns its place. Each of its three sections runs on its own [[part:automaton_core|cores]]: break a bridge and both halves fight on, but only the tail can fly.",
    lore: "The precursors grew its wards from the Lattice's own crystal. The Lattice still will not say what they were given for it.",
